    "turn_idx": 43,
    "turn_text": "and packages that have been appropriated. of the $3.5 trillion, only two trillion have gone out the door. So you have one and a half trillion in different accounts still sitting there. We should be reviewing that and looking at what's been effective and what's not been effective. So what we can do is make sure we don't repeat the mistakes. And then the proposal that the Republican majority under McConnell has made was another trillion. Some Democrats think that's not enough. I happen to look at it from the standpoint of saying, well, first of all, before I'm going to tell you whether it's enough or not enough, let me see what we've done with the first three and a half trillion if we spent two. We have one and a half left of the two. We spent what was good, what was bad, what was fraudulent, what was missed spent, and what was helpful. So there's certain ways to evaluate this. The thing that I would criticize leader, majority leader McConnell and Republican caucus is this. They're in control. They're setting the agenda. For the last two and a half months since we've had the first corona package that went out the door, he hasn't brought anybody together. He hasn't put a working team together. There hasn't been a bipartisan group officially put together. Now, there's myself and other people talking to our colleagues on the Republican side and on the Democrat side back and forth. We're not that far apart. I don't believe when you hear the rank and foul talk, but when you hear leadership, they don't even talk in each other. That's the problem. But I think they'll be forced to do something next week. I really believe it.",
