    "turn_text": "You would think, Dave, that's the prudent way and that's the adult way of doing things. It's the way it used to be done. I'm told that since I've been there, basically everything's been played through the media. The committee meetings are not what they used to be. They don't have the clout they had. It used to be when a committee met and a committee sent a bill. I didn't went to the floor. Now, whoever the majority leader, whether it's been Harry Reid or whether it's a church on a Democrat side, or an announcement from Michigan Conner for the last many years, he has the total control of what goes to before and another how it comes out of the committee. He has the total control basically on the committee and committee assignments and what the committee agenda is. Oversight, it's just unbelievable how much control is delegated in just a few people's hands, both ours and these. And I think that the committee, I think Senator should take back the power that they were invested by the Constitution and should exercise that power. And yes, we do meet. And we're meeting now just basically as a group and as a group that's meeting informally,",
