    "turn_idx": 193,
    "turn_text": "Yes. And so what they have done is, and again, they are reiterating that they also do not believe that upon investigation as much as they can, that these things have happened. But to move forward, they have updated some of their policies, specifically the client grievance policy and procedures. And this is in hopes that if somewhat, because part of the problem with the allegations that came out was that they are from the past, and it's hard to do something now and it's hard to even investigate now and it dealt with people that aren't even there anymore so in some cases and so What this is saying is they're trying to empower people that if something happens to write, then come to them. And so they've changed some of their policies, including the fact that they're implementing a hotline, which is going to allow individuals to make a complaint, do it anonymously, and do it without having to be seen in person so that it can be anonymous. And it will be operated by a third party, staff 24-7, and it is not something that you would be talking to a direct. staff member about so that you could have comfort there. The second thing that they're going to be doing is making the executive director have the power to forward complaints of discrimination, harassment, inappropriate conduct, all of these things to an independent third party to conduct investigations and provide a report of the factual findings. And if the complaint has to do with the executive director, then that will go to the board and they will do that. But somewhat, a third party will be investigating things moving forward. Should there be a complaint? And then finally, They've just changed up some of the language and added language to the client grievance policy and procedures to emphasize that if a complaint's made, there will be no retaliation. So if it comes out that you complained about something or you wanted something investigated, it's not that you will no longer be allowed in. It's not that you'll be treated poorly. Once you go there, all complaints will be taken and that person will be treated fairly. That's kind of the big. Yeah, I'd say those are the big three points that I pulled out of this.",
